course: dictionary
lesson: 11080
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning you need. Welsh is one of these words. In «Welsh cakes» and «Welsh flag», Welsh describes a thing, so it means from or to do with Wales, a country in the United Kingdom.
explain: Capital letters are clues too. The Welsh are the people of Wales, and Welsh with a capital letter can also name the language spoken there. Ask yourself: is this word describing a thing, naming a language, or naming people? The word next to it often tells you.
explain: Informal speech is different again. Jade's family ate «a Welsh stew» called cawl, so Welsh there describes the dish. Chloe in Cardiff says «lush» for lovely, and a Welsh nan's «cwtch» means a hug. These are slang words, so use them with friends, not in formal writing.
explain: The verb welsh is old-fashioned and informal. It means to break a promise to pay, and many people find this use rude, so you should not use it. If you meet it, look for clues about a deal or a debt, and check a dictionary when you are unsure.
fact: Welsh means from or to do with Wales, a country in the United Kingdom.
fact: Welsh is an old Celtic language spoken in Wales, alongside English.
fact: The Welsh are the people of Wales.
fact: Wales has the capital Cardiff, and road signs there are in both Welsh and English.
fact: «Lush» is Welsh slang for lovely, and «cwtch» means a hug.
exercise: «She ate Welsh cakes at the café in Cardiff.» What does Welsh mean in this sentence? | Made of wood | *From Wales | Very fast | A dog breed
exercise: Which word names the old Celtic language spoken in Wales, alongside English? | Cawl | Lush | Cardiff | *Welsh
exercise: Chloe says «This poem's lush, but I don't get it.» What does lush mean? | *Lovely | Wet and muddy | Very old | Broken
test: «The Welsh are friendly people, so the visitors felt at home.» Who are the Welsh in this sentence? | A stew | *The people of Wales | The language of London | A kind of cake
test: The verb «welsh» is informal and old-fashioned. What does «to welsh on a deal» mean? | To smile and wave | To cook a meal | To build a wall | *To break a promise to pay
exam: Jade's nan says «cwtch». What does it mean? | A stew | A road sign | A flag | *A hug
